.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
The clipboard, spoken to Windows directly\&. 

Installed in place of the SDL one on Windows, because Windows carries rich text in a registered format SDL has no code for\&. See the source for the whole of the reason\&.
.PP
Not part of the host facing interface, the same as the accessibility backends are not: the window installs these and nothing else calls them\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_clipboard_windows\&.h\fP\&.
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int32_t schultz_windows_clipboard_offer (void * context, const char *const * formats, uint32_t count, \fBschultz_clipboard_make_fn\fP make, void * make_context)"

.PP
Puts a set of formats on the Windows clipboard\&. Matches schultz_clipboard_offer_fn\&. The context is the window handle from schultz_windows_clipboard_owner, or NULL to let the calling task own the clipboard instead\&.
.PP
Formats are written richest first, which is the order Windows asks for: markup, then words, then a picture\&. That is the opposite of the order they arrive in, where plain text leads\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontext\fP A window handle, or NULL\&. 
.br
\fIformats\fP The media types on offer\&. 
.br
\fIcount\fP How many\&. 
.br
\fImake\fP Produces the bytes of whichever is asked for\&. 
.br
\fImake_context\fP Passed to make, unchanged\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, or SCHULTZ_ERR_UNAVAILABLE when the clipboard would not open\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const void * schultz_windows_clipboard_take (void * context, const char * format, uint64_t * out_length)"

.PP
Takes one format off the Windows clipboard\&. Matches schultz_clipboard_take_fn\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontext\fP A window handle, or NULL\&. 
.br
\fIformat\fP The media type wanted\&. 
.br
\fIout_length\fP Receives how many bytes\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The bytes, or NULL when the clipboard holds none in that format\&. Owned here and valid until the next call\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_windows_clipboard_holds (void * context, const char * format)"

.PP
